{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Every valley.</b> Since it is low, then it shall be raised. And note, גיא is not in construct state, like גיא המון גוג (Ezekiel 39:11). And it is possible that the word גיא is defective, thus and so, like מה מליל (Isaiah 21:11). And the meaning is that the returnees shall come without toil:" "<b>The crooked.</b> Like עקוב הלב (Jeremiah 17:9), and it is the opposite of plain." "<b>And the rugged places.</b> From the same root as מרכסי איש (Psalms 31:21), in the sense of a crooked place."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:01.922268020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}